    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 3/3 tests).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented owner address normalization following the codebase's established pattern of small, self-contained `@ControllerAdvice` units.\n\n**Two files touched:**\n\n1. **New** `OwnerAddressNormalizationAdvice.java` \u2014 a fresh, cohesive advice (mirroring `OwnerEmailNormalizationAdvice`) that in `afterBodyRead` rewrites the DTO's address to its canonical form: trim + collapse whitespace, upper-case, and token-wise abbreviation expansion (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). Because it mutates the DTO before persistence, the normalized value is what gets **stored and returned**. It exposes a `static normalize(...)` so other advices can reuse it \u2014 exactly as `OwnerUniqueTelephoneAdvice` reuses `OwnerTelephoneNormalizationAdvice.toE164`.\n\n2. **Two-line change** inside `OwnerUniqueHouseholdAdvice.isDuplicateHousehold` so the **address** comparison uses `OwnerAddressNormalizationAdvice.normalize`. The `lastName` keeps its own lower-case normalize on purpose \u2014 routing a name through the address normalizer would wrongly expand something like \"St John\" into \"STREET JOHN\".\n\n**Why nothing else changed:**\n- *Blank-after-normalization rejection* is already handled: a whitespace-only address is `isBlank()`, and normalization can't turn any non-blank input into blank, so the existing `OwnerFieldsValidationAdvice` rejects it with 400 \u2014 no edit needed there.\n- *Shared household id* (`OwnerMapper.householdId`) is derived from the stored address, which is now the normalized canonical form, so household members automatically share an id without touching the mapper.\n\nKeeping the surrounding complexity out of the two large classes (the mapper and the validation advice) and confining the real logic to a brand-new low-context class is what keeps the structural impact minimal.",
